course: dictionary
lesson: 3566
title: Fertilise: when new life can begin
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To fertilise means to help something start to grow. A gardener can fertilise soil by adding manure or compost so that plants grow better.
explain: In living things, fertilising is when a male cell joins a female egg cell so a new life can start. The context tells you this: «A hen lays eggs with or without a rooster; shop eggs are not fertilised, because no rooster mated with the hen, so they could never hatch.» The clue is "could never hatch": a fertilised egg can hatch, and an unfertilised one cannot.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «Even a fertilised egg must be kept at about 37 to 38 degrees for 21 days to hatch.» If fertilised means "has been joined by a male cell so a chick can start to grow", the sentence makes sense.
fact: To fertilise means to help something start to grow, or to help it grow better.
fact: To fertilise soil means to add things like manure, compost or chemicals so plants grow better.
fact: In eggs, to fertilise means a male cell joins the female egg, so a chick can start to grow.
fact: «Fertilised» in «Shop eggs are not fertilised» means they have not been joined by a male cell, so they could never hatch.
fact: A fertilised egg must be kept at about 37 to 38 degrees for 21 days to hatch.
exercise: «Shop eggs are not fertilised, because no rooster mated with the hen, so they could never hatch.» What does fertilised mean here? | Sold in a shop | Kept cold in a fridge | Cracked and broken | *Joined by a male cell, so a chick could start to grow
exercise: Dad says, «We will fertilise the lawn this spring.» What is he going to do? | Cut the grass very short | *Add food to the soil so the grass grows better | Water the grass with the hose only | Plant new trees
exercise: «A hen lays about one egg a day in good times, with or without a cockerel.» Find and copy one word that means a male chicken. | egg | hen | *cockerel | day
test: What does it mean to fertilise soil? | To wet it with rain | To cover it with stones | To dig it up and turn it over | *To add things like manure or compost so plants grow better
test: «Even a fertilised egg must be kept at about 37 to 38 degrees for 21 days to hatch.» What does a fertilised egg need to hatch? | Being sold in a shop | Being shaken every hour | Cold water for a week | *Warmth, kept at about 37 to 38 degrees for 21 days
exam: What is the best clue that fertilised means a chick could start to grow? | *No rooster mated with the hen, so they could never hatch | Eggs are sold in shops | A hen lays eggs | Shop eggs
